Patch-Id: ASTRA-0010
Title: Keep the DevTools process actor alive through toolbox teardown
Tier: P2
Upstream-Files: devtools/client/fronts/watcher.js, devtools/server/actors/watcher/ParentProcessWatcherRegistry.sys.mjs, devtools/server/connectors/js-process-actor/DevToolsProcessParent.sys.mjs
Intent: DevTools is the product's Inspect surface, and its teardown logs three uncaught errors in ESR 153 that users read as failures: NotFoundError "No such JSProcessActor 'DevToolsProcess'" (bug 2044741), and, once that is deferred, "Tried to send a 'target-destroyed-form' event on an already destroyed actor 'watcher'" / "can't access property 'cancelForwarding', watcherInfo.watcher.conn is null" at quit. The cause is ordering: the process actor is unregistered in the same turn that destroys the watcher, so in-flight requests and late process messages still look the actor up. Defer the unregistration to an idle turn (re-checking that no watcher claimed it), make the process actor tolerate a watcher that is already destroyed, and stop logging an error for a resource whose document died mid-navigation (the resource is dropped either way).
Risk: low (registration lifetime only; no protocol or target change; Toolbox behaviour is covered by the probe)
Test: forge lint; `tools/perf/stress/devtools_probe.py` (7/7 behaviour checks; upstream_noise all zero: actor errors 0, teardown 0, late-resource 0, was 6/0/3 before); stock Firefox 159 shows the same actor line without this patch
Verified-On: 153.6.0
Removal-Plan: drop when the pinned engine carries the upstream fixes (bug 2044741 and the 155 crash fix in bug 2056174); then the late-resource log line can return as upstream
---
diff --git a/devtools/client/fronts/watcher.js b/devtools/client/fronts/watcher.js
index 69cddc0e7d..99fbb4363d 100644
--- a/devtools/client/fronts/watcher.js
+++ b/devtools/client/fronts/watcher.js
@@ -205,7 +205,9 @@ class WatcherFront extends FrontClassWithSpec(watcherSpec) {
     if (topLevelTarget?.innerWindowId == innerWindowId) {
       return topLevelTarget;
     }
-    console.error("Unable to find target with innerWindowId:" + innerWindowId);
+    // A resource can outlive the document it belongs to: resources emitted
+    // just before a navigation can be handled after the document's target was
+    // destroyed. There is no target to attribute them to, which is expected.
     return null;
   }
 
diff --git a/devtools/server/actors/watcher/ParentProcessWatcherRegistry.sys.mjs b/devtools/server/actors/watcher/ParentProcessWatcherRegistry.sys.mjs
index 8229bea142..f76c006a12 100644
--- a/devtools/server/actors/watcher/ParentProcessWatcherRegistry.sys.mjs
+++ b/devtools/server/actors/watcher/ParentProcessWatcherRegistry.sys.mjs
@@ -243,8 +243,16 @@ export const ParentProcessWatcherRegistry = {
    */
   maybeUnregisterJSActors() {
     if (sessionDataByWatcherActor.size == 0) {
-      unregisterBrowserToolboxJSProcessActor();
-      unregisterJSProcessActor();
+      // Unregistering here races the teardown that just removed the watcher:
+      // in-flight requests still ask for the process actor and throw
+      // NotFoundError. Finish the current turn first, then unregister if no
+      // new watcher claimed it in the meantime.
+      Services.tm.idleDispatchToMainThread(() => {
+        if (sessionDataByWatcherActor.size == 0) {
+          unregisterBrowserToolboxJSProcessActor();
+          unregisterJSProcessActor();
+        }
+      });
     }
   },
 
